  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support evidence-based, private sector and community engagement for migration management in Bosnia and Herzegovina</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project titled Support Evidence-Based, Private Sector and Community Engagement for Migration Management in Bosnia and Herzegovina aims to address the triple challenge of migration in Bosnia and Herzegovina (BiH). The country faces significant emigration, sectoral labour shortages, and ongoing mixed migration of thousands of migrants transiting through BiH. The project is aligned with national, regional, EU, and global frameworks and strategies, including the EU enlargement process and the BiH Strategy on Migration and Asylum 2021-2025. It aims to support evidence-based policy-making and administrative processes for comprehensive approach to regular and irregular migration management in BiH, including private sector and community-based engagement. The project has a focus on data collection, analysis, and the production of actionable recommendations to strengthen the capacities of BiH authorities to understand and manage migration. It also works to create alternatives to irregular migration, ensuring the rights of migrant workers in line with EU and international standards and strengthens resource provision to migrants and government capacities to enhance regular mobility pathways and improve social systems&apos; capacities and responsiveness to the specific needs of labour migrants and host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
